# The Go sources, the shell scripts, the package payloads under root/ and the
# OpenWrt config files under files/ are all consumed on Linux, so keep LF in
# the working tree as well as in the index -- the latter is all core.autocrlf
# guarantees.
#
# This is not cosmetic. A CRLF in an installed script makes the shebang read
# "/bin/sh\r", which the kernel reports as a bad interpreter: an error naming a
# path that plainly exists. Anyone cloning on Windows with core.autocrlf=true
# would otherwise build packages whose helper scripts cannot run. It also makes
# gofmt -l flag every file, which turns the CI formatting gate into noise.
* text=auto eol=lf
